A kit jump that a logged landing launched before it doesn't contradict (engine drivers.ts replayCast `contradicted`).

What it does: the replay drops a kit jump whose skipped part holds a logged landing (JUMPDROP). A detached hit whose
launch (KitHit.launch) comes before the jump lands whatever the jump does (schedule.ts jumpCast keeps it), so such a
landing shows nothing about the jump; the diff leaves it out of `skipped`. Case: f8793bc8aea2 93.98 s, Laevatain's
empowered battle skill, whose Magma Fragment ticks (an ability entity's, launched at frame 4) are logged across its
jump 30 → 80: the jump was dropped and the cast ran its un-jumped timeline (its empowered hit still lands, pinned).

Measured 2026-11-27 (measure --base HEAD --split files, this part alone on 107766a): no development, earlier-pending or
verified log moved; one hold-out worse (plain −23, assumed +8, fallback +15; totals, operator keys 2, kinds basic,
battle, status). Dropped: right by the data, but it moves only a hold-out, for the worse, and nothing in the
development logs explains how. Likely a Laevatain hold-out where the dropped jump hid a misplacement (as f879's
87.12 s cast did before logcasts.ts onEntityClock); to re-measure once a development log shows the case.

